1. Check docker version : docker -version
2. Check kubernetes version and it's cluster : kubectl version --client
3. Build image of E7 - docker build -t docker-app:1.0 .
4. Create deployment.yaml
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: docker-app
spec:
  replicas: 2
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: docker-app
template:
  metadata:
    labels:
      app: docker-app
spec:
  containers:
    - name: docker-app
    image: docker-app:1.0
    imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent
    ports:
      - containerPort: 5000

5.Deploy the application : kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml
6. Check the deployment : kubectl get deployments
7. Check the pods : kubectl get pods 
8. Create a Kuberenetes service : service.yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: docker-app-service
spec:
  type: NodePort
  selector:
    app: docker-app
  ports:
    - protocol: TCP
    port: 5000
    targetPort: 5000

9. Apply the service kubectl apply -f service.yaml
10. Check services : kubectl get services
11. Access the application : kubectl get service docker-app-service
12. It is accessed through port forwarding : kubectl port-forward service/docker-app-service 5000:500
13. Open http://localhost:5000
